 "triggers": [
  {
   "mark": "wall_view",
   "id": "wall_view",
   "say": "The wall of the plateau, up close: a face of dry-laid stone with the square ends of timber beams showing every few feet, nailed together inside with iron spikes as long as your forearm, and earth heaped behind it all. Fire won't burn it and a ram won't shake it. The gate turns in between two horns of wall, so anyone who comes at it is boxed in on three sides."
  },
  {
   "mark": "camp_view",
   "id": "camp_view",
   "say": "The levy camp smells of wet wool and smoke. These are the men the elders wouldn't let into the council: herdsmen, debtors, younger sons, runaways. Vercingetorix gave them spears and a name. They would die for him. Some of them are going to."
  }
 ]
